  "id": "COMPOUND:40454 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Nudifloside B is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets, primarily CD276 antigen. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which converge on CD276 as a central mediator. The CD276 antigen is recognized by the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in epigenetic regulation. The presence of multiple targets, including Taiwanin E Methyl Ether and Decane, further underscores the potential for Nudifloside B to interact with the PRC2 complex through different molecular mechanisms. These findings suggest that Nudifloside B may act as a modulator of the PRC2 complex, potentially influencing gene expression through the CD276 antigen. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of CD276 as a critical node in the interaction network, emphasizing its importance in linking Nudifloside B to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
